<title>USA: Summit Properties Inc acquires apartments.</title>
<headline>Summit Properties Inc acquires apartments.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLOTTE, N.C. 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summit Properties Inc said on Tuesday it purchased a luxury apartment community in Broward County, Florida for a total purchase price of $28 million, or $87,000 per apartment home.</p>
<p>The company funded the acquisition with proceeds from the sale of  315,029 shares of common stock at a price of $21.625 per share ($6,812,500) and its unsecured line of credit.</p>
<p>Charlotte-based Summit Properties Inc designs, develops and manages luxury apartment communities.</p>
